==Prefectures==
Harujima is divided into twelve prefectures, each with its own distinct character, economy, and cultural identity. These range from the hyper-dense Okami Metropolis to the vast, mountainous wilderness of Ishiwara Prefecture.

===Okami Metropolis (OK-01)===
{{main|Okami Metropolis}}
The Okami Metropolis is the political, economic, and cultural heart of Okaiken. With a population of 17,257,969, it is by far the most populous prefecture on the island and the nation. The metropolis encompasses the national capital, [[Okami]], which serves as the seat of the [[Wisteria Throne]] and the [[Diet of Okaiken|Diet]]. The metropolitan area spans 1,687.15 km², yielding an extraordinary population density of over 10,000 persons per square kilometre. The city's core is situated on the [[Sendai Plain]], where the Okachi River provides the immense water supply necessary to sustain the urban agglomeration.

The metropolis is divided into 35 administrative wards, the most populous being the central Okami ward (8,259,189), followed by Mitsu-Minato (1,388,670) and Hojo (725,669). The metropolis also administers the remote [[Kazan Islands]] chain to the south, including Chichijima, Hahajima, and Ioto, as well as the isolated Okinotorishima atoll. Okami is the primary hub for the nation's digital infrastructure, housing the headquarters of [[Kizan Systems]], the corporation providing the hardware backbone for the nationwide [[Satori AI]] network.

