===Miyagi Prefecture (OK-02)===
{{main|Miyagi Prefecture}}
Miyagi Prefecture occupies the northern coast of Harujima, facing the straits that separate Okaiken from the sovereign state of [[Yanbaru]]. With a population of 3,395,239 and an area of 5,716.40 km², it is the second most populous prefecture on the island. Its capital, [[Shinagawa]], is the northern terminus of the [[Harujima Shinkansen]] and a major deep-water port. The prefecture is renowned for its hot, humid tropical climate, making it one of the most popular beach and resort destinations in the country. It is also known for its exports in premium spirits, tropical fruits, and the celebrated {{nihongo|[[Miyagi-buta]]|宮城豚|Miyagi-buta}}, a heritage breed black pork that has become one of Okaiken's most prestigious luxury food exports.

The prefecture's history is defined by the "Pirate Coast" era, when the rugged coastline served as a sanctuary for the infamous Sea Wolves. The Tejima trading post, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, stands as a testament to the limited foreign contact maintained during the Honda Shogunate's isolation period. In modern times, the coastal corridor around Shinagawa has earned the nickname "The Silicon Strait" ({{nihongo|シリコン海峡|Shirikon Kaikyō}}), reflecting its concentration of maritime robotics and renewable energy research facilities.

